{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YXzGrsysdGRKpFRqB4tPTg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport type { MosaicColor, MosaicDocument, MosaicEngineContext, MosaicSource } from \"@m0saic/types\";\n2\timport { asTemplateId } from \"@m0saic/types\";\n3\timport { toM0String } from \"@m0saic/dsl-stdlib\";\n4\timport { bindProp, bindPropPath, defineMosaicTemplate, definePropsSchema, makeColorTile, placeInsetPieces, tag, wrapMeasured } from \"@m0saic/template-utils\";\n5\timport type { LayoutConstraint, RelationalConstraint } from \"@m0saic/template-utils\";\n6\timport { textFitsMeasured, withLayoutIntent } from \"../../../_shared/layout\";\n7\timport { budget, textCell, widthOf } from \"../../../_shared/text\";\n8\timport { whyTutorial } from \"../../../_shared/why\";\n9\timport type { WhySpec } from \"../../../_shared/why\";\n10\t\n11\t/**\n12\t * `@one-a-day/sports/cubing-average-card/v1` - one speedcubing average as a\n13\t * card: the solves as bars, the dropped best and worst in parentheses with a\n14\t * hollow bar, the average as the headline, and the delta against the old PB.\n15\t *\n16\t * ONE CONCEPT: the headline is COMPUTED, and the dropped solves stay on the\n17\t * card. The user gives the solves; the count decides the kind (3 is a Mo3, 5\n18\t * an Ao5, 12 an Ao12), so a \"Mo3\" label over five solves cannot happen. The\n19\t * best and the worst are dropped (Ao5, Ao12), printed in parentheses and\n20\t * drawn hollow; the average is the mean of what is left. Each bar says what\n21\t * the footnote says: its distance from the average (`bar: \"spread\"`, the\n22\t * default: left = faster, who carried the average and who dragged it) or its\n23\t * length from zero (`bar: \"length\"`, the slowest fills the track, where a\n24\t * 24-32 second session draws five near-identical bars).\n25\t *\n26\t * The rule that bites: all arithmetic is integer hundredths of a second. The\n27\t * average is rounded to the nearest hund